{%- comment -%}
One TRMNL markup for all three calendar views. It branches on `view` in the
payload, so every instance gets the same markup and only the Polling URL differs:

  day        https://cal.lsck0.dev/<token>/day.json
  tomorrow   https://cal.lsck0.dev/<token>/day-next.json
  this week  https://cal.lsck0.dev/<token>/week.json
  last week  https://cal.lsck0.dev/<token>/week-prev.json
  next week  https://cal.lsck0.dev/<token>/week-next.json
  month      https://cal.lsck0.dev/<token>/month.json
  next month https://cal.lsck0.dev/<token>/month-next.json

Exactly ONE url per instance: TRMNL merges several into one payload for one
screen, which breaks the top-level keys and cannot give you separate screens.

Overlapping events are positioned, not listed: calendar-sync packs each day's
clashes into lanes and ships top/height/left/width percentages, because Liquid
cannot do the interval arithmetic. Two things at once sit side by side.

The source is named in words on each block. An earlier version also coded it
into the left border style, which was unreadable at this size and mislabelled
itself anyway, so the border is now uniform.

Kept flat, one tag per line. Do not run "Fix indentation" on it.
{%- endcomment -%}

<style>
/* TRMNL's own .layout centres and pads a single child, which rendered the day
   view as a narrow column floating in the middle of the screen. This plugin
   draws a full-bleed grid, so neutralise that wrapper. */
.layout { display: block !important; width: 100% !important; height: 100% !important; padding: 0 !important; margin: 0 !important; }
/* Fill the box we are given, not the viewport. 100vh was wrong because the
   markup editor previews in a container far taller than it is tall: the rows
   stretched past the visible area and only three of the month's six weeks
   fitted. 100% tracks whatever TRMNL hands us, and min-height keeps the
   layout from collapsing if that parent turns out to have no definite
   height, which is what made an earlier version render blank. max-height
   keeps the content clear of the title bar, which is drawn over the page. */
.cal { display: flex; flex-direction: column; height: 100%; min-height: 422px; max-height: calc(100vh - 58px); width: 100%; gap: 0; padding: 8px 10px 4px; box-sizing: border-box; }
.cal-row { display: flex; gap: 6px; flex: 1 1 auto; min-height: 0; }
/* the all-day band sits between the headers and the grid, so it needs the
   same hairline separating it from both */
.tg-row--allday { border-top: 1px solid #c8c8c8; }

/* ---- shared event chip ----------------------------------------------
   One rule down the left edge rather than a box: a 2px frame around every
   block turned a busy week into a grid of boxes inside boxes, and on e-ink
   the frames read louder than the titles they hold. */
.ev { border-left: 4px solid #000; padding: 0 0 1px 5px; overflow: hidden; background: #fff; }
.ev-t { font-size: 17px; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
.ev-s { font-size: 19px; line-height: 1.12; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
.ev-m { font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.15; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
.ev-src { font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .10em; text-transform: uppercase; }

/* ---- time grid (day + week) ------------------------------------------
   Three rows that share one column template, so the hour axis and the event
   area are the same box. Previously the axis spanned the full height while
   events were positioned inside a shorter body below the day header, so every
   block was drawn at the wrong time.

   The columns are separated by hairlines inside one outer frame instead of
   each carrying its own border, so the week reads as a single grid. */
.tg-row { display: flex; width: 100%; }
.tg-row--grid { flex: 1 1 auto; min-height: 0; border-top: 2px solid #000; }
.tg-gutter { width: 46px; flex: 0 0 46px; }
.tg-gutter--label { font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .08em; align-self: center; text-align: right; padding-right: 6px; }
/* one line each, capped: "Flo Abwesend (Studium)" wrapped to five lines per
   day and pushed the time grid down to a third of the screen. */
.tg-row--allday { flex: 0 0 auto; max-height: 52px; overflow: hidden; }
.tg-axis { position: relative; }
.tg-h { position: absolute; right: 6px; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .02em; transform: translateY(-50%); color: #555; }
/* the first label sits on the grid's top edge, where half of it would be
   cut off by the frame; hang it below the line instead of centred on it */
.tg-h--first { transform: none; }

.tg-hd { flex: 1 1 0; min-width: 0; display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 5px; padding: 0 6px 3px; }
.tg-dow { font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #555; }
.tg-dom { font-size: 25px; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
/* today is the one thing worth picking out, so mark the number and nothing
   else; a filled header cell drew the eye to the whole column instead. */
.tg-hd--today .tg-dow { color: #000; }
.tg-hd--today .tg-dom { background: #000; color: #fff; padding: 0 6px 2px; }

.tg-adcell { flex: 1 1 0; min-width: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1px; padding: 2px 4px; overflow: hidden; }
.tg-adcell + .tg-adcell, .tg-col + .tg-col { border-left: 1px solid #c8c8c8; }
.tg-adcell .ev { padding: 0 0 0 5px; border-left-width: 3px; }
.tg-adcell .ev-s { display: block; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.2; white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; }
.tg-adcell .ev-m { font-size: 12px; }

.tg-col { position: relative; flex: 1 1 0; min-width: 0; overflow: hidden; }
.tg-col--weekend { background: #f4f4f4; }
.tg-line { position: absolute; left: 0; right: 0; border-top: 1px solid #ededed; }
.tg-line--major { border-top-color: #c4c4c4; }

/* Events are the only filled shapes on the grid, so they carry the weight:
   a thick left rule and a hairline body, not a box. */
.tg-ev { position: absolute; box-sizing: border-box; border: 1px solid #909090; border-left: 5px solid #000; padding: 0 3px; overflow: hidden; background: #fff; display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: center; line-height: 1.06; }
.tg-ev .ev-t { font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; white-space: nowrap; flex: 0 0 auto; }
/* do not let the title shrink away: the source line below it would win the
   space and the block would show a time and a category but no event. */
/* one line: three lines of text only fit a 90-minute block if the title
   is one of them, and a wrapped title pushed the source out of the box. */
.tg-ev .ev-s { font-size: 13px; flex: 0 0 auto; display: -webkit-box; -webkit-line-clamp: 1; -webkit-box-orient: vertical; overflow: hidden; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }

.tg-ev .ev-src { font-size: 10px; flex: 0 0 auto; white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; color: #555; }
/* calendar-sync already grew every block to a readable minimum and pushed
   the later ones down, so the height here is honest and no min-height is
   needed; thin edges keep the one line inside it. */
.tg-ev--compact { justify-content: flex-start; }
.tg-ev--compact .ev-s { display: block; font-size: 11px; line-height: 1.2; white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; }
/* the day view has one wide column, so put it all on a single readable row */
.tg-ev--wide { flex-direction: row; align-items: center; gap: 10px; border-left-width: 7px; }
.tg-ev--wide .ev-t { font-size: 19px; flex: 0 0 auto; }
.tg-ev--wide .ev-s { font-size: 22px; -webkit-line-clamp: 1; flex: 1 1 auto; }
.tg-ev--wide .ev-src { font-size: 13px; flex: 0 0 auto; margin-left: auto; }

/* ---- month ----------------------------------------------------------- */
.mo { display: flex; flex-direction: column; flex: 1 1 auto; width: 100%; min-height: 0; box-sizing: border-box; border-top: 2px solid #000; }
.mo-dows { display: flex; padding-bottom: 3px; }
.mo-dow { flex: 1 1 0; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; text-align: center; color: #555; }
/* hairlines inside one frame, like the week grid: a 2px box per cell turned
   the month into 42 boxes and buried the four that had anything in them. */
.mo-wk { display: flex; flex: 1 1 0; min-height: 0; }
.mo-wk + .mo-wk { border-top: 1px solid #c8c8c8; }
.mo-cell { flex: 1 1 0; min-width: 0; padding: 2px 5px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1px; overflow: hidden; }
.mo-cell + .mo-cell { border-left: 1px solid #c8c8c8; }
.mo-cell--other .mo-n { color: #b4b4b4; }
.mo-cell--other .mo-e { color: #909090; border-left-color: #b4b4b4; }
.mo-cell--weekend { background: #f4f4f4; }
.mo-n { font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.1; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
.mo-cell--today .mo-n { background: #000; color: #fff; padding: 1px 6px 2px; align-self: flex-start; }
.mo-e { font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.24; border-left: 3px solid #000; padding-left: 4px; white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; }
.mo-more { font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; color: #555; }
</style>

{% if view == 'month' %}
<div class="layout">
<div class="cal">
<div class="mo">
<div class="mo-dows">
<span class="mo-dow">Mon</span><span class="mo-dow">Tue</span><span class="mo-dow">Wed</span><span class="mo-dow">Thu</span><span class="mo-dow">Fri</span><span class="mo-dow">Sat</span><span class="mo-dow">Sun</span>
</div>
{% for wk in weeks %}
<div class="mo-wk">
{% for d in wk.days %}
<div class="mo-cell{% if d.is_today %} mo-cell--today{% endif %}{% if d.other_month %} mo-cell--other{% endif %}{% if d.is_weekend %} mo-cell--weekend{% endif %}">
<span class="mo-n">{{ d.day }}</span>
{% for ev in d.events %}
<div class="mo-e">{% unless ev.all_day %}<b>{{ ev.time }}</b> {% endunless %}{{ ev.summary }}</div>
{% endfor %}
{% if d.more > 0 %}<div class="mo-more">+{{ d.more }} more</div>{% endif %}
</div>
{% endfor %}
</div>
{% endfor %}
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="title_bar">
<span class="title">{{ label }}</span>
<span class="instance">{{ total_events }} {% if total_events == 1 %}event{% else %}events{% endif %}</span>
</div>

{% elsif view == 'day' or view == 'week' %}
{% assign is_day = false %}{% assign wide = '' %}{% if view == 'day' %}{% assign is_day = true %}{% assign wide = ' tg-ev--wide' %}{% endif %}
<div class="layout">
<div class="cal">

<div class="tg-row tg-row--head">
<div class="tg-gutter"></div>
{% for d in days %}
<div class="tg-hd{% if d.is_today %} tg-hd--today{% endif %}"><span class="tg-dow">{{ d.weekday }}</span><span class="tg-dom">{{ d.day }}</span></div>
{% endfor %}
</div>

{% if has_all_day %}
<div class="tg-row tg-row--allday">
<div class="tg-gutter tg-gutter--label">all day</div>
{% for d in days %}
<div class="tg-adcell">
{% for ev in d.all_day_events %}
<div class="ev"><span class="ev-s">{{ ev.summary }}</span></div>
{% endfor %}
{% if d.all_day_more > 0 %}<div class="ev-m"><b>+{{ d.all_day_more }} more</b></div>{% endif %}
</div>
{% endfor %}
</div>
{% endif %}

<div class="tg-row tg-row--grid">
<div class="tg-gutter tg-axis">
{% for h in grid.hours %}
{% if view == 'day' or h.major %}<div class="tg-h{% if forloop.first %} tg-h--first{% endif %}" style="top:{{ h.top_pct }}%">{{ h.label }}</div>{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
</div>
{% for d in days %}
<div class="tg-col{% if d.is_today %} tg-col--today{% endif %}{% if d.weekday == 'Sat' or d.weekday == 'Sun' %} tg-col--weekend{% endif %}">
{% for h in grid.hours %}
<div class="tg-line{% if h.major %} tg-line--major{% endif %}" style="top:{{ h.top_pct }}%"></div>
{% endfor %}
{% for ev in d.timed_events %}
<div class="tg-ev{{ wide }}{% unless is_day %}{% if ev.compact %} tg-ev--compact{% endif %}{% endunless %}" style="top:{{ ev.top_pct }}%;height:{{ ev.height_pct }}%;left:{{ ev.left_pct }}%;width:{{ ev.width_pct }}%">
{% if is_day %}
<div class="ev-t">{{ ev.time }}&ndash;{{ ev.end_time }}</div>
<div class="ev-s">{{ ev.summary }}</div>
<div class="ev-m ev-src">{{ ev.source_label }}</div>
{% elsif ev.compact %}
<div class="ev-s"><b>{{ ev.time }}</b> {{ ev.summary }}</div>
{% else %}
<div class="ev-t">{{ ev.time }}</div>
<div class="ev-s">{{ ev.summary }}</div>
{% if ev.tall %}<div class="ev-m ev-src">{{ ev.source_label }}</div>{% endif %}
{% endif %}
</div>
{% endfor %}
</div>
{% endfor %}
</div>

</div>
</div>
<div class="title_bar">
<span class="title">{% if view == 'day' %}{{ weekday }}{% elsif offset == 0 %}This week{% elsif offset == -1 %}Last week{% elsif offset == 1 %}Next week{% else %}Week {{ week_number }}{% endif %}</span>
<span class="instance">{{ label }} &middot; {{ total_events }} {% if total_events == 1 %}event{% else %}events{% endif %}{% if later > 0 %} &middot; {{ later }} outside {{ grid.start_label }}&ndash;{{ grid.end_label }}{% endif %}{% if max_overlap > 1 %} &middot; up to {{ max_overlap }} at once{% endif %}</span>
</div>

{% else %}
<div class="layout">
<div class="markdown">
<span class="title">Calendar: no data</span>
<div class="content">No `view` in the payload. Check the plugin's Polling URL points at one of day.json / week.json / month.json on cal.lsck0.dev.</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="title_bar"><span class="title">Calendar</span><span class="instance">waiting for data</span></div>
{% endif %}
